WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.168
One night soon after James had left Birtwick Park for his new job, I was awakened from a sound sleep by the clang of the stable bell.

2
00:00:12.169 --> 00:00:14.066
John came running in.

3
00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:18.140
His clothes were askew as if he'd pulled them on very quickly.

4
00:00:18.141 --> 00:00:23.748
"Wake up, Beauty!" he called. "You must go as fast as you can!"

5
00:00:23.749 --> 00:00:29.010
Almost before I knew what was happening, he had my saddle and bridle on.

6
00:00:29.011 --> 00:00:34.085
Then he led me out and jogged me over toward the main house.

7
00:00:34.086 --> 00:00:38.639
The squire was standing in the doorway wrapped in a robe.

8
00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:43.375
"Ride for your life, John," he said in a hoarse, anxious voice.

9
00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:48.286
"Or rather, ride for your mistress' life. There's not a moment to lose.

10
00:00:48.287 --> 00:00:53.067
Give Dr. White this note, and then give your horse a rest at the inn.

11
00:00:53.068 --> 00:00:55.974
After that start back as soon as you can."

12
00:00:55.975 --> 00:00:59.814
John took the note from the squire and put it in his pocket.

13
00:00:59.815 --> 00:01:04.242
"Yes, sir," he said. "We'll ride swiftly!"

14
00:01:04.243 --> 00:01:09.454
He swung into the saddle, urging me into a trot as we passed through the gates.

15
00:01:09.455 --> 00:01:14.964
Once we were out on the road, he touched my side with his heel, asking me to canter.

16
00:01:14.965 --> 00:01:20.473
I was fully awake by now and feeling extra alert due to the unusual situation.

17
00:01:20.474 --> 00:01:23.918
It was a moonlit night and almost as bright as day.

18
00:01:23.919 --> 00:01:28.774
Everything looked and felt a little different than it did in the daytime.

19
00:01:28.775 --> 00:01:34.410
Still I knew that John would take care of me and so I wasn't afraid.

20
00:01:34.411 --> 00:01:38.939
Soon we came to a long, level stretch of road along the river.

21
00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:42.886
"Now, Beauty," John said, "do your best."

22
00:01:42.887 --> 00:01:47.754
He closed his legs against my side, and I understood instantly what he wanted.

23
00:01:47.755 --> 00:01:50.828
Stretching my legs, I burst into a gallop.

24
00:01:50.829 --> 00:01:54.454
For the next two miles I ran as fast as I could.

25
00:01:54.455 --> 00:01:58.145
Even my racehorse ancestors couldn't have done any better!

26
00:01:58.146 --> 00:02:02.800
When we reached a bridge, John pulled me back to a trot and patted me.

27
00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:07.440
"Well done, Beauty!" he said. "Good boy!"

28
00:02:07.441 --> 00:02:11.997
On the other side of the bridge, John seemed willing to continue at the trot.

29
00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:17.455
But it was a clear, frosty night, and I was still feeling good and ready to run.

30
00:02:17.456 --> 00:02:22.137
When I moved into a canter, and then a gallop, he allowed me to do so.

31
00:02:22.138 --> 00:02:27.279
We passed through a sleepy village and continued on our way.

32
00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:30.843
After eight miles we finally reached the larger town.

33
00:02:30.844 --> 00:02:35.509
It was very quiet, and my hooves clattered on the pavement.

34
00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:39.688
John steered me toward a street near the market square.

35
00:02:39.689 --> 00:02:44.694
The church clock struck three as we stopped outside the doctor's house.

36
00:02:44.695 --> 00:02:48.642
John rang the bell twice, and then knocked loudly on the door.

37
00:02:48.643 --> 00:02:51.469
An upstairs window slid open.

38
00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:56.857
"What is it?" Dr. White called down, sounding sleepy.

39
00:02:56.858 --> 00:03:00.852
"Mrs. Gordon is very ill, sir," John called back.

40
00:03:00.853 --> 00:03:04.981
"The squire is afraid she'll die if you don't come right away."

41
00:03:04.982 --> 00:03:08.258
"I'll be right down," the doctor said.

42
00:03:08.259 --> 00:03:10.456
The window slid shut again.

43
00:03:10.457 --> 00:03:16.136
Moments later Dr. White was hurrying out toward us, buttoning his coat.

44
00:03:16.137 --> 00:03:19.660
"There's just one problem," he told John.

45
00:03:19.661 --> 00:03:25.171
"My son had to go somewhere tonight and took my horse. Can I ride yours?"

46
00:03:25.172 --> 00:03:27.332
John gave me a worried look.

47
00:03:27.333 --> 00:03:32.109
"He came at a gallop almost the whole way, sir," he told the doctor.

48
00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:35.105
"I was going to let him rest before heading back.

49
00:03:35.106 --> 00:03:39.356
But I suppose the squire would want you to take him if there's no other choice."

50
00:03:39.357 --> 00:03:42.246
Soon the doctor was climbing into the saddle.

51
00:03:42.247 --> 00:03:46.911
I don't wish to say too much about our ride back to Birtwick Park.

52
00:03:46.912 --> 00:03:50.978
The doctor was heavier than John, and not as good a rider.

53
00:03:50.979 --> 00:03:55.737
For those reasons the second eight miles felt much longer than the first.

54
00:03:55.738 --> 00:04:00.929
But I did my very best, galloping as fast as I could for most of the way.

55
00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:05.900
When we came to a steep hill, Dr. White brought me down to a walk.

56
00:04:05.901 --> 00:04:10.067
"All right, boy," he said kindly, giving me a pat.

57
00:04:10.068 --> 00:04:12.966
"Take a breath here before we go on."

58
00:04:12.967 --> 00:04:18.231
Once we reached the top of the hill, all he had to do was touch my sides with his heels.

59
00:04:18.232 --> 00:04:21.520
Then I was off again at a run.

60
00:04:21.521 --> 00:04:24.547
The squire was waiting for us when we got back.

61
00:04:24.548 --> 00:04:29.899
Little Joe stood nearby, yawning and looking sleepy.

62
00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:35.027
The doctor jumped down and hurried into the house with the squire.

63
00:04:35.028 --> 00:04:40.207
But I had no energy to watch them go. I was dead tired.

64
00:04:40.208 --> 00:04:44.433
"Come on, Black Beauty," Little Joe said as he took me by the bridle.

65
00:04:44.434 --> 00:04:49.088
"John won't be back for a while since he has to walk the whole way home.

66
00:04:49.089 --> 00:04:55.631
But don't worry, I'll take good care of you."

